From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:00:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo: keep the UFS
 clocks at 300 MHz

With UFS clock scaling the host drops core_clk/core_clk_unipro to 37.5 MHz when idle and switches
the gear down with them; on the Duo's UFS the link then never returns to HS-G3 (I/O errors, then
a dead disk). Pinning both clocks at their maximum (freq-table-hz min = max) leaves devfreq
nothing to scale, so the gear never changes, while every other UFS power-saving feature
(clock gating, hibern8, runtime suspend) stays on.

This replaces a machine-compatible check in ufs-qcom, which also stopped matching when the
phone's own bootloader (ABL) replaces the root compatible string. Tested on both boot paths
(UEFI and ABL): 3 rounds of 512 MB write/read with idle periods, 0 UFS errors.

This patch was written by Claude (Anthropic's AI assistant) under the direction of Bryson, who reviewed and
tested it on a Surface Duo.

Signed-off-by: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../dts/qcom/sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo.dts    | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo.dts
index cae283a78..a884aca5b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo.dts
@@ -502,6 +502,22 @@ &ufs_mem_hc {
 	vccq-max-microamp = <700000>;
 	vccq2-supply = <&vreg_s4a_1p8>;
 	vccq2-max-microamp = <750000>;
+
+	/*
+	 * Keep core_clk and core_clk_unipro at 300 MHz: with the 37.5 MHz floor the
+	 * host's clock scaling drops the link out of HS-G3 and it never comes back.
+	 * min = max leaves devfreq nothing to scale.
+	 */
+	freq-table-hz =
+		<300000000 300000000>,
+		<0 0>,
+		<0 0>,
+		<300000000 300000000>,
+		<0 0>,
+		<0 0>,
+		<0 0>,
+		<0 0>,
+		<0 300000000>;
 };
 
 &ufs_mem_phy {
